d crew cooperation (concern for others) while B's memory issue and D's mood are bigger concerns.\n\nLet's do that: state current recommendation Candidate C, reference Agent1's B recommendation and Agent2's D recommendation, bring in evidence for C, explain why C may be better overall.\n\nWe must ensure we use explicit facts from our notes: C can make correct decisions quickly; C has excellent attention skills; C puts concern for others above everything; C difficulty communicating ideas; C regarded as egocentric; C not very willing to further his education.\n\nWe also need to address criteria: decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, stress resilience (not mentioned for C, but we can note quick decisions imply calm under pressure). We must not infer beyond facts. We can say quick decisions indicate ability to handle crisis, but that's inference; maybe safe to say \"can make correct decisions quickly\" suggests decision quality under pressure.\n\nOk.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C."}
